{
  "uid": "registration-case",
  "title": "Registration Case",
  "description": "Three registration paths share one database pool and one outbox/Kafka/Compliance flow. Async and batched HTTP responses mean RabbitMQ acceptance; sync returns after a direct commit. Processing-to-commit p95 includes database waits and excludes queue and batch collection waiting. Batched items each measure the full shared transaction duration, not duration divided by batch size. One-second sampling, ten-second rates and rolling thirty-second histogram estimates; lifetime counters reset on restart.",
  "tags": [
    "registration-case"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "refresh": "1s",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 11,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-5m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": []
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Configuration and current activity",
      "description": "Rabbit consumers is configured per queue: the ordinary async queue and batch queue each have this many consumers. All paths share the Registry database pool. The displayed prefetch is for the ordinary queue; effective batch prefetch is max(configured prefetch, batch size). Batch size is a maximum; partial batches also flush on the collection timeout. Busy work includes database waiting and is not CPU parallelism. Compliance concurrency is also bounded by Kafka partitions.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 3
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(max(registry_config_consumers{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Rabbit consumers / queue",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "(max(registry_config_prefetch{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Normal queue prefetch",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "(sum(hikaricp_connections_max{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Registry pool max",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "expr": "(max(registry_threads_virtual_enabled{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Virtual threads",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "E",
          "expr": "(max(compliance_config_concurrency{job=\"compliance\",application=\"compliance-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"compliance\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Compliance consumers",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "F",
          "expr": "(sum(compliance_workers_active{job=\"compliance\",application=\"compliance-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"compliance\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Compliance busy now",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "G",
          "expr": "(max(registry_config_batch_size{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Max registrations / batch",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "noValue": "No data",
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Virtual threads"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "mappings",
                "value": [
                  {
                    "type": "value",
                    "options": {
                      "0": {
                        "text": "OFF"
                      },
                      "1": {
                        "text": "ON"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Server decisions and processing /s",
      "description": "Ten-second rate estimates from application counters sampled every second, not exact k6 burst throughput. Async and batched accepted decisions follow RabbitMQ broker confirmation. Sync completed decisions follow a direct Registry transaction and include replays. Registry creations and Compliance checks count new committed results. These stages can finish at different times.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 3,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 12
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(sum(rate(registry_intake_requests_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",outcome=\"accepted\"}[10s]))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Async accepted decisions",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "(sum(rate(registry_sync_requests_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",outcome=~\"created|replayed\"}[10s]))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Sync completed decisions",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "(sum(rate(registry_registrations_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",outcome=\"created\"}[10s]))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Registry creations",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "expr": "(sum(rate(compliance_events_total{job=\"compliance\",application=\"compliance-service\",outcome=\"processed\"}[10s]))) and on() (max(up{job=\"compliance\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Compliance checks",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "E",
          "expr": "(sum(rate(registry_batch_intake_requests_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",outcome=\"accepted\"}[10s]))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Batched accepted decisions",
          "instant": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 3,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "interval": "1s"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "RabbitMQ queues (async and batched)",
      "description": "Current unfinished work in the ordinary and batched queues, not total messages handled. Direct sync bypasses both. Ready messages wait at the broker; unacknowledged includes processing, prefetch and batch collection. RabbitMQ updates these statistics every five seconds by default; one-second Prometheus scrapes cannot recover queue peaks between broker updates. A short run can show zero depth despite thousands of messages passing through. Check acceptance, Registry creations and average DB batch size alongside this graph. Batch prefetch is at least batch size. Both ready and unacknowledged must drain to zero. Missing telemetry stays a gap.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 3,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 12
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(sum(rabbitmq_queue_messages_ready{job=\"rabbitmq\",queue=\"registration.commands\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"rabbitmq\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Async: ready at broker",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "(sum(rabbitmq_queue_messages_unacked{job=\"rabbitmq\",queue=\"registration.commands\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"rabbitmq\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Async: unacknowledged",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "(sum(rabbitmq_queue_messages_ready{job=\"rabbitmq\",queue=\"registration.commands.batched\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"rabbitmq\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Batched: ready at broker",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "expr": "(sum(rabbitmq_queue_messages_unacked{job=\"rabbitmq\",queue=\"registration.commands.batched\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"rabbitmq\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Batched: unacknowledged",
          "instant": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 3,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "interval": "1s"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Registry processing and database pool",
      "description": "One-second samples. Processing workers includes direct HTTP requests and Rabbit worker attempts, including time waiting for a database connection. This total is not bounded by Rabbit consumer count. All three paths share Hikari: active connections are borrowed; pending callers wait for one. One batch worker can process several registrations in one transaction; the worker count is not a registration count or CPU parallelism. Short activity between samples can be missed.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 15,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 12
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(sum(registry_workers_active{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Processing workers (incl. DB waits)",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "(sum(hikaricp_connections_active{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Active DB connections",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "(sum(hikaricp_connections_pending{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Waiting for DB connection",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "expr": "(sum(hikaricp_connections_max{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Pool maximum",
          "instant": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 3,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Pool maximum"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "fill": "dash",
                  "dash": [
                    6,
                    4
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.lineWidth",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "interval": "1s"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "HTTP response time (p95, milliseconds)",
      "description": "Successful HTTP responses over a rolling 30-second window. Async and batched return after RabbitMQ confirms acceptance; processing can continue afterward. Sync returns after its direct Registry transaction commits. These responses promise different things: a lower queued response time does not mean a faster database write. Histogram estimates can differ from exact per-run k6 measurements. Idle windows remain gaps.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 15,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 12
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(1000 * histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_bucket{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",uri=\"/registrations\",method=\"POST\",status=\"202\"}[30s])))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Async: accepted into RabbitMQ (202)",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "(1000 * histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_bucket{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",uri=\"/registrations/sync\",method=\"POST\",status=~\"200|201\"}[30s])))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Sync: Registry DB committed (200/201)",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "(1000 * histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_bucket{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",uri=\"/registrations/batched\",method=\"POST\",status=\"202\"}[30s])))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Batched: accepted into RabbitMQ (202)",
          "instant": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 3,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisPlacement": "left",
            "axisLabel": "HTTP response (milliseconds)"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Async: accepted into RabbitMQ (202)"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "green"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Sync: Registry DB committed (200/201)"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "yellow"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Batched: accepted into RabbitMQ (202)"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "purple"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "interval": "1s"
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Registry processing to commit (p95, milliseconds)",
      "description": "All three modes measure successful new registrations from processor entry until user and outbox commit, including database connection waiting. Excludes HTTP admission, normalization, Rabbit queue and batch collection waiting, retry backoff, Kafka and Compliance. For successful bulk commits, each new registration records the full shared transaction duration, not duration divided by batch size. Individual isolation commits also appear under batched mode; recovery forwarded to the ordinary queue appears under async mode. Batch registration latency can rise while registrations committed per second improves. Replays and failures are excluded. Modes can have different concurrency limits. Rolling thirty-second p95 estimates can blend nearby runs; idle windows stay gaps.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 27,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 10
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(1000 * histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(registry_registration_processing_seconds_bucket{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",mode=\"sync\"}[30s])))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Direct /sync: processing to commit",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "(1000 * histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(registry_registration_processing_seconds_bucket{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",mode=\"async\"}[30s])))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Async worker: processing to commit",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "(1000 * histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(registry_registration_processing_seconds_bucket{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",mode=\"batched\"}[30s])))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Batched worker: processing to commit",
          "instant": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 3,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisPlacement": "left",
            "axisLabel": "Registry processing to commit (milliseconds)"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Direct /sync: processing to commit"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "yellow"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Async worker: processing to commit"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "green"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Batched worker: processing to commit"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "purple"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ],
          "width": 360
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "interval": "1s"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Progress since each service started",
      "description": "Application decision and result counters since each service process started, not totals for the selected range or an exact per-run ledger. Async/batched accepted and sync completed are server decisions; sync includes replay responses. Registry creations count new users, while Compliance checks count new results. Services reset independently on restart, so these values need not match. Use the HTML k6 report for a specific run. Average new users per DB batch is a lifetime average for successful bulk commits; failed batches and individual fallback commits are excluded.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 37,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(sum(registry_intake_requests_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",outcome=\"accepted\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Async accepted",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "(sum(registry_sync_requests_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",outcome=~\"created|replayed\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Sync completed",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "(sum(registry_registrations_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",outcome=\"created\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Registry creations",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "expr": "(sum(compliance_events_total{job=\"compliance\",application=\"compliance-service\",outcome=\"processed\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"compliance\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Compliance checks",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "E",
          "expr": "(sum(registry_batch_intake_requests_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",outcome=\"accepted\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Batched accepted",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "F",
          "expr": "(sum(registry_batch_size_sum{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"}) / (sum(registry_batch_size_count{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"}) > 0)) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Avg new users / DB batch",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "noValue": "No data",
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Avg new users / DB batch"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "none"
              },
              {
                "id": "decimals",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Errors since each service started",
      "description": "Counters since each service started. HTTP 4xx/5xx includes validation errors, conflicts and 503 responses; a timeout can have an unknown outcome. Failed attempts can be retried. Dead-letter values count publishes, not current queue depth. Services reset independently. An absent HTTP error counter is zero only while Registry is UP; unavailable telemetry remains No data.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 37,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "((sum(http_server_requests_seconds_count{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",uri=~\"/registrations(/sync|/batched)?\",method=\"POST\",status=~\"[45]..\"})) or on() vector(0)) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "HTTP 4xx/5xx",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "(sum(registry_registrations_failures_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Registry failed attempts",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "(sum(registry_registrations_dead_lettered_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Registry dead letters",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "expr": "(sum(compliance_events_dead_lettered_total{job=\"compliance\",application=\"compliance-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"compliance\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Compliance dead letters",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "decimals": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "noValue": "No data",
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Operational checks",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 41,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Scrape reachability",
      "description": "Prometheus scrape reachability only: UP means the metrics endpoint answered, not that registrations, Kafka or CDC are healthy. DOWN means a configured target failed its scrape. UNKNOWN means no up series exists for that job. No success guard hides DOWN states.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 42,
        "w": 18,
        "h": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(up{job=\"registry\"}) or on() vector(-1)",
          "legendFormat": "Registry",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "max(up{job=\"compliance\"}) or on() vector(-1)",
          "legendFormat": "Compliance",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "max(up{job=\"rabbitmq\"}) or on() vector(-1)",
          "legendFormat": "RabbitMQ",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "decimals": 0,
          "min": -1,
          "noValue": "UNKNOWN",
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "-1": {
                  "text": "UNKNOWN",
                  "color": "gray"
                },
                "0": {
                  "text": "DOWN",
                  "color": "red"
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "UP",
                  "color": "green"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "special",
              "options": {
                "match": "null",
                "result": {
                  "text": "UNKNOWN",
                  "color": "gray"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "max": 1,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "gray",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Registry DLQ depth (current)",
      "description": "Messages currently remaining in registration.commands.dlq: READY plus delivered/unacknowledged. This is current depth, not the lifetime dead-letter publication counter. Any positive depth is red. Missing queue series or an unreachable RabbitMQ scrape remain UNKNOWN; there is no zero fallback.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 18,
        "y": 42,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(sum(rabbitmq_queue_messages_ready{job=\"rabbitmq\",queue=\"registration.commands.dlq\"}) + sum(rabbitmq_queue_messages_unacked{job=\"rabbitmq\",queue=\"registration.commands.dlq\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"rabbitmq\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "DLQ messages",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "noValue": "UNKNOWN",
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "special",
              "options": {
                "match": "null",
                "result": {
                  "text": "UNKNOWN",
                  "color": "gray"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Kafka fetch-position lag (records)",
      "description": "Sum of observed nonnegative client fetch-position lag for the exact topic outbox.event.user. This excludes dotted/underscored topic-label aliases and uses current lag, not rolling lag_max values. Fetch lag is not committed-offset lag or unfinished business work: zero does not prove every Compliance result committed. Missing, negative or NaN samples remain gaps, and an unreachable Compliance scrape hides stale values.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 46,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(sum(kafka_consumer_fetch_manager_records_lag{job=\"compliance\",application=\"compliance-service\",topic=\"outbox.event.user\"} >= 0)) and on() (max(up{job=\"compliance\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Observed fetch-position lag",
          "instant": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 3,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisPlacement": "left"
          },
          "noValue": "No data",
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "interval": "1s"
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Errors per second",
      "description": "Ten-second rates, not lifetime totals or counts for one benchmark run. HTTP 5xx covers all three registration POST endpoints; Registry failed attempts count technical processing failures and can overlap HTTP failures or retried async work, so do not add the lines. Rates handle counter resets. HTTP error labels are created on first occurrence: rates need two samples and can undercount an initial short burst. The Registry failed-attempt counter is pre-initialized. An absent HTTP 5xx series is treated as zero only while Registry is UP; a failed scrape remains a gap.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 46,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "((sum(rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",uri=~\"/registrations(/sync|/batched)?\",method=\"POST\",status=~\"5..\"}[10s]))) or on() vector(0)) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "HTTP 5xx /s",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "(sum(rate(registry_registrations_failures_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"}[10s]))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Registry failed attempts /s",
          "instant": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 3,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisPlacement": "left"
          },
          "noValue": "No data",
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "interval": "1s"
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "JVM diagnostics",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 55,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "collapsed": true,
      "panels": [
        {
          "id": 15,
          "type": "timeseries",
          "title": "JVM heap used (%)",
          "description": "Heap used as a percentage of the available reported heap maximum, separately for each application process. Used bytes include all heap pools; the denominator sums only positive maximums because G1 Eden/Survivor can report -1. Allocation and collection normally make this fluctuate; growth alone does not establish a leak. Missing memory metrics or an unreachable application scrape remain gaps.",
          "gridPos": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 56,
            "w": 12,
            "h": 9
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "targets": [
            {
              "refId": "A",
              "expr": "(100 * sum by (job) (jvm_memory_used_bytes{job=~\"registry|compliance\",area=\"heap\"}) / sum by (job) (jvm_memory_max_bytes{job=~\"registry|compliance\",area=\"heap\"} > 0)) and on(job) (max by (job) (up{job=~\"registry|compliance\"}) == 1)",
              "legendFormat": "{{job}} heap used",
              "instant": false
            }
          ],
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "percent",
              "min": 0,
              "color": {
                "mode": "palette-classic"
              },
              "custom": {
                "drawStyle": "line",
                "lineInterpolation": "linear",
                "lineWidth": 2,
                "fillOpacity": 3,
                "showPoints": "never",
                "spanNulls": false,
                "axisCenteredZero": false,
                "axisPlacement": "left"
              },
              "noValue": "No data",
              "max": 100,
              "decimals": 1
            },
            "overrides": []
          },
          "options": {
            "legend": {
              "displayMode": "table",
              "placement": "bottom",
              "calcs": [
                "lastNotNull",
                "max"
              ]
            },
            "tooltip": {
              "mode": "multi",
              "sort": "desc"
            }
          },
          "interval": "1s"
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "type": "timeseries",
          "title": "GC pause time (%)",
          "description": "Percentage of wall-clock time recorded as GC pauses, averaged over 30 seconds for each application. Computed as 100 times the rate of cumulative jvm_gc_pause_seconds_sum. This is pause time, not CPU utilization and not an individual pause duration. Missing GC series or an unreachable application scrape remain gaps; no observations are invented.",
          "gridPos": {
            "x": 12,
            "y": 56,
            "w": 12,
            "h": 9
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "targets": [
            {
              "refId": "A",
              "expr": "(100 * sum by (job) (rate(jvm_gc_pause_seconds_sum{job=~\"registry|compliance\"}[30s]))) and on(job) (max by (job) (up{job=~\"registry|compliance\"}) == 1)",
              "legendFormat": "{{job}} GC pause time",
              "instant": false
            }
          ],
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "percent",
              "min": 0,
              "color": {
                "mode": "palette-classic"
              },
              "custom": {
                "drawStyle": "line",
                "lineInterpolation": "linear",
                "lineWidth": 2,
                "fillOpacity": 3,
                "showPoints": "never",
                "spanNulls": false,
                "axisCenteredZero": false,
                "axisPlacement": "left"
              },
              "noValue": "No data",
              "decimals": 2
            },
            "overrides": []
          },
          "options": {
            "legend": {
              "displayMode": "table",
              "placement": "bottom",
              "calcs": [
                "lastNotNull",
                "max"
              ]
            },
            "tooltip": {
              "mode": "multi",
              "sort": "desc"
            }
          },
          "interval": "1s"
        }
      ]
    }
